{"title":"2005 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the area enclosed by the graph of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/6/dc6fef6dd077cc39c7492faf4b54d56bb0d6f867.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|3x|+|4y|=12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"122\" height=\"18\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/1/ba1f027368b47d6fb691fecb0153478eec7f4da0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)}\\ 6      \\qquad \\mathrm{(B)}\\ 12      \\qquad \\mathrm{(C)}\\ 16      \\qquad \\mathrm{(D)}\\ 24      \\qquad \\mathrm{(E)}\\ 25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"378\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If we get rid of the absolute values, we are left with the following 4 equations (using the logic that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/e/8de907587d0f88e2cc674171d292d80c0098eabd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|a|=b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"18\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/a/2fa30e2beb1820f6b39f6251023709c8165cefc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-b$\" width=\"22\" height=\"12\" />):\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/4/9c40c481511750766f665255f34ffe39e8459a0a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 3x+4y=12 \\\\ -3x+4y=12 \\\\ 3x-4y=12 \\\\ -3x-4y=12 \\end{align*}\" width=\"114\" height=\"91\" />\n</p><p>We can then put these equations in slope-intercept form in order to graph them.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/0/860d1524c5b2f1300856502c58fb854953e3045e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 3x+4y=12 \\,\\implies\\, y=-\\dfrac{3}{4}x+3\\\\ -3x+4y=12\\,\\implies\\, y=\\dfrac{3}{4}x+3\\\\ 3x-4y=12\\,\\implies\\, y=\\dfrac{3}{4}x-3\\\\ -3x-4y=12\\,\\implies\\, y=-\\dfrac{3}{4}x-3\\end{align*}\" width=\"273\" height=\"167\" />\n</p><p>Now you can graph the lines to find the shape of the graph:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/9/a19def037694543a1771b3897d68d519dd066fcf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] Label f;  f.p=fontsize(6);  xaxis(-8,8,Ticks(f, 4.0));  yaxis(-6,6,Ticks(f, 3.0));  fill((0,-3)--(4,0)--(0,3)--(-4,0)--cycle,grey); draw((-4,-6)--(8,3), Arrows(4)); draw((4,-6)--(-8,3), Arrows(4)); draw((-4,6)--(8,-3), Arrows(4)); draw((4,6)--(-8,-3), Arrows(4));[/asy]\" width=\"668\" height=\"505\" />\n</p><p>We can easily see that it is a rhombus with diagonals of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. The area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/e/a2e04b8013c8e3230eb2ae243c30cf41d562af3d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{1}{2}\\times 6\\times8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"78\" height=\"38\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/6/1260e1f36eef835a548a3bef2d39b52af3aa4189.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\mathrm{(D)}\\ 24}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"63\" height=\"29\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>You can also assign <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Then you can easily see that the diagonals are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Multiply and divide by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to get D. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The graph is symmetric with respect to both coordinate axes, and in the first quadrant it coincides with the graph of the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/7/157aaf716d5598966d900aa7a85a6ffb1869e1e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x + 4y = 12.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"106\" height=\"16\" /> Therefore the region is a rhombus, and the area is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/0/ef0949e38da672b8251f851ec7d51ec63056bfa9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\text{Area} = 4\\left(\\frac{1}{2}(4\\cdot 3)\\right) = 24 \\rightarrow \\boxed{D}\\]\" width=\"253\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/f/f6fb4f11d88c24aa05f736f273aa28bf02060d80.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw((-5,0)--(5,0),Arrow); draw((0,-4)--(0,4),Arrow); label(&quot;$x$&quot;,(5,0),S); label(&quot;$y$&quot;,(0,4),E); label(&quot;4&quot;,(4,0),S); label(&quot;-4&quot;,(-4,0),S); label(&quot;3&quot;,(0,3),NW); label(&quot;-3&quot;,(0,-3),SW); draw((4,0)--(0,3)--(-4,0)--(0,-3)--cycle,linewidth(0.7)); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"205\" />\n</p><p>~Alcumus\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12B\" title=\"2005 AMC 12B\">2005 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2005 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2005 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2005 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1